1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,629
The second attempt was designed to answer a question about life rather than about money: what should a person feel when the work he built is handed to somebody else?

2
00:00:09,629 --> 00:00:14,038
“He himself shall decide,” the director said.

3
00:00:14,038 --> 00:00:16,947
“She herself shall decide.

4
00:00:16,947 --> 00:00:21,766
And the future will refer to neither of them by name.”

5
00:00:21,766 --> 00:00:27,910
The behavior of the two friends was studied by a psychologist during the whole week.

6
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:31,929
“Affect is not character,” she warned.

7
00:00:31,929 --> 00:00:41,796
“A circumstance can make an honest person behave badly, and a reform can make a bad habit look like a moral choice.”

8
00:00:41,796 --> 00:00:46,040
The complex part was the appointment of a successor.

9
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:52,499
“We retain the responsibility and we appoint the accountability,” the auditor said.

10
00:00:52,499 --> 00:01:01,317
“The alternative is a psychological knot: anxiety about the fate of the archive and no authority over it.”

11
00:01:01,317 --> 00:01:04,831
The psychology of the pair was striking.

12
00:01:04,831 --> 00:01:10,739
“Every automatic click of the mouse carries an ethic inside it,” Lin said.

13
00:01:10,739 --> 00:01:23,381
“The ethics of a small team are embedded in its habits, not in its rules.” A corruption of the process would be visible only to a reader with a conscience.

14
00:01:23,381 --> 00:01:33,943
The optional parts of the handover were the souvenir, the kite, the yoga mat, and the stormy letter of resignation that nobody sent.

15
00:01:33,943 --> 00:01:44,641
“An idealistic plan and a liver complaint have the same effect on a schedule,” Maya wrote, and the joke landed because it was true.

16
00:01:44,641 --> 00:01:53,034
The second attempt consisted of one page, one signature, and one rule that the friends agreed to obey under pressure.

17
00:01:53,034 --> 00:02:00,542
The age of the project was now part of its value, and the water in the well was still the same water.

18
00:02:00,542 --> 00:02:08,270
It was important to dream of a secure archive; the evil was not in the ambition but in the corruption of it.

19
00:02:08,270 --> 00:02:16,483
The air, the water, and the well were the same as before, and the process was the only thing under our control.

20
00:02:16,483 --> 00:02:24,700
These things we never said out loud: that we had thought about leaving, and that the win mattered less than the method.

21
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:30,679
During the second year the authority to appoint was ours, and now it is not.

22
00:02:30,679 --> 00:02:36,733
Under it all lay a simple fact, and it was just as true the second time.

23
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:43,655
We had to find a way into the live archive, and it was left to us.
